---
const siteUrl = "https://kalinduwijekoon.com";
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="description" content="Cloud Security Engineer portfolio focused on resilient cloud platforms, detection engineering, and practical security automation.">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#08111f">
  <meta property="og:title" content="Cloud Security Engineer | Portfolio">
  <meta property="og:description" content="A practical cloud security portfolio for engineering teams in Germany.">
  <meta property="og:type" content="website">
  <meta property="og:url" content={`${siteUrl}/`}>
  <title>Cloud Security Engineer | Portfolio</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css">
</head>
<body>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a>
  <header class="site-header">
    <nav class="nav shell" aria-label="Primary navigation">
      <a class="brand" href="#top" aria-label="Home">
        <span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true">K</span>
        <span>Cloud<span class="brand-accent">Sec</span></span>
      </a>
      <button class="nav-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="nav-links">Menu</button>
      <div class="nav-links" id="nav-links">
        <a href="#focus">Focus</a>
        <a href="#work">Selected work</a>
        <a href="#approach">Approach</a>
        <a class="nav-cta" href="mailto:hello@example.com">Let's connect <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="hero shell" id="top">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> Open to Cloud Security opportunities in Germany</p>
        <h1>Secure the cloud.<br><em>Enable the team.</em></h1>
        <p class="hero-summary">Cloud security engineering with a bias toward useful guardrails, measurable detection, and infrastructure that developers can trust.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="#work">Explore selected work <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
          <a class="text-link" href="mailto:hello@example.com">Get in touch <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-aside" aria-label="Current focus">
        <div class="terminal-card">
          <div class="terminal-top"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span class="terminal-label">security_context.yml</span></div>
          <div class="terminal-body">
            <p><span class="code-muted">profile:</span> <span class="code-value">cloud_security_engineer</span></p>
            <p><span class="code-muted">location:</span> <span class="code-value">Germany / EU</span></p>
            <p><span class="code-muted">default:</span> <span class="code-value">secure_by_design</span></p>
            <p><span class="code-muted">signal:</span> <span class="code-green">● systems_online</span></p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="metric-row">
          <div><strong>03</strong><span>security domains</span></div>
          <div><strong>∞</strong><span>learning mindset</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ticker" aria-label="Areas of practice">
      <div class="ticker-track">
        <span>Cloud security</span><i>✦</i><span>Detection engineering</span><i>✦</i><span>DevSecOps</span><i>✦</i><span>Identity architecture</span><i>✦</i><span>Cloud security</span><i>✦</i><span>Detection engineering</span>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section shell" id="focus">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">01 / What I focus on</p>
        <h2>Security that makes<br><em>momentum possible.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="focus-grid">
        <article class="focus-card focus-card-featured">
          <span class="card-number">01</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Cloud foundations</h3>
            <p>Designing landing zones, identity boundaries, logging, and policy guardrails that scale with the organization.</p>
            <ul class="tag-list"><li>AWS / Azure</li><li>IAM</li><li>Policy as code</li></ul>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="focus-card">
          <span class="card-number">02</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Detection & response</h3>
            <p>Turning cloud telemetry into useful signals, triage playbooks, and response workflows that reduce uncertainty.</p>
            <ul class="tag-list"><li>SIEM</li><li>Threat detection</li><li>Incident response</li></ul>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="focus-card">
          <span class="card-number">03</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Secure delivery</h3>
            <p>Embedding security checks into CI/CD so teams find issues early without slowing down delivery.</p>
            <ul class="tag-list"><li>GitHub Actions</li><li>IaC scanning</li><li>Supply chain</li></ul>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-dark" id="work">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-heading section-heading-light">
          <p class="eyebrow">02 / Selected work</p>
          <h2>Proof over <em>promises.</em></h2>
          <p class="section-intro">Sample case studies for the portfolio. Replace these with your own labs, assessments, and measurable outcomes.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="work-list">
          <article class="work-item">
            <div class="work-index">01</div>
            <div class="work-content">
              <p class="work-kicker">Cloud governance · AWS</p>
              <h3>Guardrails without friction</h3>
              <p>A reference landing zone that combines least-privilege access, centralized audit trails, and preventive controls with a clear developer path.</p>
              <a class="work-link" href="mailto:hello@example.com?subject=Cloud%20governance%20case%20study">Discuss the approach <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
            </div>
            <div class="work-visual visual-grid" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
          </article>
          <article class="work-item">
            <div class="work-index">02</div>
            <div class="work-content">
              <p class="work-kicker">Detection engineering · CloudTrail</p>
              <h3>From noisy logs to signals</h3>
              <p>A detection pack for suspicious identity activity, with tested hypotheses, severity context, and response notes for an on-call team.</p>
              <a class="work-link" href="mailto:hello@example.com?subject=Detection%20engineering%20case%20study">Discuss the approach <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
            </div>
            <div class="work-visual visual-pulse" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
          </article>
          <article class="work-item">
            <div class="work-index">03</div>
            <div class="work-content">
              <p class="work-kicker">DevSecOps · GitHub Actions</p>
              <h3>Security in the pull request</h3>
              <p>A lightweight pipeline for secrets, dependencies, infrastructure, and container checks with actionable developer feedback.</p>
              <a class="work-link" href="mailto:hello@example.com?subject=DevSecOps%20case%20study">Discuss the approach <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
            </div>
            <div class="work-visual visual-bars" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section shell approach-section" id="approach">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">03 / My approach</p>
        <h2>Clear thinking.<br><em>Practical outcomes.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="approach-grid">
        <div class="approach-copy">
          <p class="lead">Good security engineering is not a gate at the end of delivery. It is a set of well-designed decisions that help a team move with confidence.</p>
          <p>I work from threat models and real operational constraints, then turn them into controls people can understand, automate, and improve. The goal is a safer system and a stronger engineering culture.</p>
          <a class="button button-dark" href="mailto:hello@example.com">Start a conversation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
        <ol class="principles">
          <li><span>01</span><div><strong>Understand the system</strong><p>Map assets, identities, data flows, and the risks that matter to the business.</p></div></li>
          <li><span>02</span><div><strong>Reduce the blast radius</strong><p>Prefer small, composable controls over brittle security theatre.</p></div></li>
          <li><span>03</span><div><strong>Make the secure path easy</strong><p>Build feedback loops and defaults that work with the team, not against it.</p></div></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cta-section">
      <div class="shell cta-inner">
        <p class="eyebrow">Have a meaningful security problem?</p>
        <h2>Let's make the cloud<br><em>safer to move fast in.</em></h2>
        <a class="button button-primary" href="mailto:hello@example.com">hello@example.com <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="site-footer">
    <div class="shell footer-inner">
      <span>© <span id="year">2026</span> CloudSec portfolio</span>
      <span>Built with care · Based in Europe</span>
      <a href="#top">Back to top ↑</a>
    </div>
  </footer>
  <script src="/script.js" defer></script>
</body>
</html>
